---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="About — Eric Brookfield" description="About Eric Brookfield's writing, AI use, and authorship standards.">
<main class="editorial-container">
  <article class="article-wrapper" style="max-width:720px;margin:0 auto;padding:var(--spacing-xl) var(--spacing-md);">
    <header class="article-header" style="margin-bottom:var(--spacing-lg);padding-bottom:var(--spacing-md);border-bottom:1px solid var(--color-rule);">
      <h1>About this site</h1>
    </header>

    <div style="font-size:clamp(1rem,1.15vw,1.0625rem);line-height:1.75;color:var(--color-text-muted);">
      <p><strong>Eric Brookfield</strong> — engineer, builder, writer, father.</p>

      <h2 style="font-size:1.375rem;margin-top:var(--spacing-lg);margin-bottom:var(--spacing-sm);color:var(--color-text);">On AI and writing</h2>

      <p>I use generative AI extensively — for research, for software development, for exploration, analysis, editing, and creative collaboration. It’s a real tool, not a magic wand, and I treat it that way.</p>

      <p>Writing published under my name should be writing I meaningfully authored and stand behind. AI involvement doesn’t itself negate authorship; I direct, edit, and sign off on everything here. Where that standard isn’t met — where a piece was substantially generated by AI rather than authored by me — I’ll try to disclose it.</p>

      <p>That’s the short version. <a href="/2026/08/26/confessional-booth.html" style="color:var(--color-accent);text-decoration:underline;">Confessional Booth</a> is where I talk through how I got here, what changed, and what the withdrawal process looks like.</p>

      <hr />

      <p style="font-family:var(--font-mono);font-size:var(--text-mono);color:var(--color-text-muted);text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.06em;">This is a living statement — updated as the practice changes.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</main>
</Layout>
